First, find $\frac{1}{4}$ of 60:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{4} \times 60 &= \frac{60}{4} = 15.
\end{align*}
Next, find $\frac{1}{5}$ of 15:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{5} \times 15 &= \frac{15}{5} = 3.
\end{align*}
Finally, find $\frac{1}{3}$ of 3:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{3} \times 3 &= \frac{3}{3} = 1.
\end{align*}
Thus, $\frac{1}{3}$ of $\frac{1}{4}$ of $\frac{1}{5}$ of 60 equals 1.
\boxed{1}

