chains:
The circumference of the base of the cylinder is \(12\) inches, so the radius of the base is \(\frac{12}{2\pi}\) inches. The height of the cylinder is \(5\) inches. The stripe winds around the cylinder exactly once, so it is essentially a helix that connects the bottom to the top of the cylinder. To find the length of the stripe, we can use the Pythagorean theorem. The horizontal distance traveled by the stripe is the circumference of the cylinder, which is \(12\) inches. The vertical distance traveled by the stripe is the height of the cylinder, which is \(5\) inches. Using the Pythagorean theorem: \[
\text{length} = \sqrt{(\text{horizontal distance})^2 + (\text{vertical distance})^2}
\] \[
\text{length} = \sqrt{12^2 + 5^2} = \sqrt{144 + 25} = \sqrt{169} = 13
\] Therefore, the length of the stripe is \(\boxed{13}\) inches.The length of the stripe is \(13\) inches.

\boxed{13}

