To expand the product of $(x+2)(x+5)$, we use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):
\begin{align*}
(x+2)(x+5) &= x \cdot x + x \cdot 5 + 2 \cdot x + 2 \cdot 5 \\
&= x^2 + 5x + 2x + 10 \\
&= x^2 + 7x + 10.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the expanded form is $x^2 + 7x + 10$.
\boxed{x^2 + 7x + 10}

